{
  "title": "Pascal's Triangle II",
  "description": "Return row number `row_index` of Pascal's triangle, counting the top row `[1]` as row `0`.\n\nEach row starts and ends with `1`, and every other entry is the sum of the two entries directly above it in the previous row.\n\n### Examples\n\n| `row_index` | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `0` | `[1]` |\n| `1` | `[1, 1]` |\n| `3` | `[1, 3, 3, 1]` |\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `0 <= row_index <= 33`\n- Every value fits in a 32-bit signed integer. Try to use only `O(row_index)` extra memory.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "vector<int> pascals_row(int row_index) {\n    vector<int> row(row_index + 1, 1);\n    for (int r = 1; r <= row_index; ++r) {\n        for (int c = r - 1; c >= 1; --c) {\n            row[c] += row[c - 1];\n        }\n    }\n    return row;\n}\n",
  "template": "vector<int> pascals_row(int row_index) {\n    // Return row row_index of Pascal's triangle (row 0 is [1]).\n    return {};\n}\n",
